---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---
<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section>
    <h2>About this site</h2>
    <p>Lenovo Graphics Pad captures Android input on a native surface and can send digitizer reports through USB HID FunctionFS or Classic Bluetooth HID. USB uses the Android USB gadget path; Bluetooth uses the system HID Device profile. Bluetooth Low Energy HID is not the transport implemented here.</p>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>Hardware and compatibility status</h3>
      <p>The tested Lenovo TB-8505F exposes touchscreen input but no active stylus source. Touch contact can provide basic binary input; continuous stylus pressure has not been verified. Windows, macOS, and specific drawing applications still require host testing, so this project is not presented as a Wacom replacement.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h3>How it works</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Source in <code>/astro</code></li>
        <li>Build uses <code>npm run build</code> to generate a static <code>dist/</code> folder</li>
        <li>CI workflow deploys <code>dist/</code> to GitHub Pages when a GitHub Release is published (or on manual dispatch)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
